  "_comment": "THE 2009 COMMITTEE DRAFT'S 8.9 RESERVED AND 8.10 CONTEXT-SENSITIVE WORD LISTS (kb/Work PB4297), transcribed from ISO/IEC 1989:20xx CD 1.2 (E) of 2009-08-23 (P3 of kb/Work PB3602 'Sources'; 8.9 on its printed pages 154-156, 8.10 on 157-159). It is a draft of the 2014 standard, not the standard, so scripts/gen-reserved-words.ps1 reads it for ONE question only: a word GnuCOBOL's cobol2014.words reserves that the draft knows (a 1985 reserved word, or a word of either list here) is NOT reserved at 2014 when neither the draft's 8.9 nor the 2023 8.9 lists it. A word the 2014 final added after the draft (the FLOAT-BINARY-n renames, PHYSICAL) keeps GnuCOBOL's flag. The words are facts; no text of the standard is held. ReservedWordsDriftTests holds this file to the generated table. CONTENT-FILTER RULE: never print this file into a conversation.",
